 **Edge Cases and Pitfalls**
 *   **Out-of-bounds coordinates:** The method explicitly handles coordinates outside the valid local range by clamping to the texture boundary, preventing undefined behavior [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Dark Edge Artifacts:** Using bounded sampling (like BBSplat) with standard 2DGS opacity causes dark edge artifacts because color decays from the center. This method prevents this by ensuring equal weights across the four bilinear corners, relying solely on 2DGS opacity for alpha fall-off [S1, unofficial].
