 ### Subtopics
-*   **2D Texture-Based Volume Rendering:** Maps 2D textures onto volume primitives. Differs by using direct bilinear interpolation with border clamping rather than other mapping strategies. Choose when smooth texture transitions across primitive boundaries are required. [Link](916-2d-texture-based-volume-rendering.md)
-*   **Palette Texture Volume Rendering:** Uses palette index lookup for color mapping. Differs by avoiding direct color interpolation in favor of quantized palette access. Choose when memory bandwidth is limited or color quantization is desired. [Link](6502-palette-texture-volume-rendering.md)
-*   **Cabral Texture Mapping:** Applies Cabral's geometric mapping approach. Differs by using a different coordinate transformation and sampling logic compared to the bilinear border-clamping approach. Choose when specific geometric mapping properties of Cabral's method are required. [Link](7257-cabral-texture-mapping.md)
-*   **Wall Surface Projection & Texture Mapping:** Projects textures onto planar wall-like surfaces. Differs by focusing on planar projection rather than primitive-local bilinear sampling. Choose for architectural or planar scene reconstruction. [Link](9883-wall-surface-projection-texture-mapping.md)
-*   **TileTrees:** Uses a hierarchical tiling structure for texture storage. Differs by organizing texture data spatially rather than sampling a flat 2D array directly. Choose when hierarchical LOD management is needed. [Link](17466-tiletrees.md)
-*   **Adapted Coordinate Texture (ACT) Module:** Adapts coordinate systems for texture mapping. Differs by dynamically adjusting coordinates rather than using fixed local-to-pixel transformation. Choose when coordinate adaptation is required for specific geometries. [Link](19576-adapted-coordinate-texture-act-module.md)
-*   **Projective Texture Mapping:** Maps textures using projective geometry. Differs by applying projective transformations rather than affine local-to-pixel scaling. Choose when perspective-correct projection is necessary. [Link](19668-projective-texture-mapping.md)
